  "body": "The same way, WebUSB added `connect` and `disconnect` events (https://github.com/reillyeon/webusb/commit/5806adfc523ff5146bc9fa883367b024d1d62699), it would be nice to have them in WebBluetooth so that Web Apps can detect connected/disconnected devices.\n\nJust some ideas there there...\n\n``` js\nnavigator.bluetooth.addEventListener('connectGatt', handleGattServer);\nnavigator.bluetooth.addEventListener('disconnectGatt', handleGattServer);\n\nfunction handleGattServer(event) {\n  var gattServer = target.value;\n  console.log('Gatt Server connected: ', gattServer.connected);\n}\n```\n\nor \n\n``` js\nnavigator.bluetooth.requestDevice({filters:[{services:['battery_service']}]})\n.then(device => device.connectGatt())\n.then(gattServer => {\n  gattServer.addEventListener('disconnect', handleGattServer);\n  // Not sure about the use of \"connect\" there...\n  gattServer.addEventListener('connect', handleGattServer);\n});\n\nfunction handleGattServer(event) {\n  var gattServer = target.value;\n  console.log('Gatt Server connected: ', gattServer.connected);\n}\n```\n",
